  "findings": [
    "The 714 ms preview completed four bounded passes and depth 48 before its 800 ms deadline, yet reported only the heart-four goal. This does not prove infeasibility.",
    "The earlier three recorded releases report both light T and heart four; reported solver times are 261, 429 and 235 ms.",
    "Primary hard-shape focus was limited to spinner boards containing thorns. This preview has a spinner and no thorns.",
    "Endpoint/path-specific candidates can share the same color layout, but previously each repeated full shared-phase evaluation.",
    "The reported predicted board contains a light T at zero-based cells 9,10,11,16,22 bordering spinner 15. Its light phase violates the existing conservative same-color-border policy; this observation does not claim that the neighboring spinner must be a sixth actually removed orb.",
    "Six dynamic spinner cells can leave a goal without any phase-stable template. Previously stable hint filtering could give that goal no primary-pass guidance even though alternate per-phase templates were still evaluated exactly."
  ],
  "source_changes": [
    "Extend the existing primary hard-shape focus to spinner multi-shape boards without requiring thorn cells.",
    "Add a per-solve 4096-slot evaluation cache with full-cell equality and pass invalidation. Contact damage/heart gating remain per-route.",
    "Record evaluationCalls and evaluationCacheHits separately from candidates; no extra time or step budget and no new spinner-touch policy.",
    "Add an unrun old/new comparison driver for the initial four recorded boards plus the retained six-spinner miss, using the existing independent all-phase probe and optional evaluation counters compatible with the older header.",
    "When a goal has no stable pattern for any permitted target color, retain its per-phase shape hints from the primary pass; this neither asserts feasibility nor relaxes exact all-phase evaluation."
  ],
